Showing the latest entries first in the value help. Loading data only when the user clicks Go, instead of fetching everything when the dialog opens.

Both can be achieved with a few annotations:
@𝗖𝗼𝗻𝘀𝘂𝗺𝗽𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻.𝘃𝗮𝗹𝘂𝗲𝗛𝗲𝗹𝗽𝗗𝗲𝗳𝗮𝘂𝗹𝘁.𝗳𝗲𝘁𝗰𝗵𝗩𝗮𝗹𝘂𝗲𝘀
 • #ON_EXPLICIT_REQUEST loads data only when the user clicks Go (default in OData V2).
 • #AUTOMATICALLY_WHEN_DISPLAYED fetches data automatically when the value help dialog is opened (default in OData V4).

@𝗨𝗜.𝗽𝗿𝗲𝘀𝗲𝗻𝘁𝗮𝘁𝗶𝗼𝗻𝗩𝗮𝗿𝗶𝗮𝗻𝘁
 • Defines the default sorting behavior for the value help results.
 • In this example, entries are sorted in descending order based on FieldFromCDS.

@Consumption.valueHelpDefault.fetchValues: #ON_EXPLICIT_REQUEST
@UI.presentationVariant: [{
    sortOrder: [{
        by: 'FieldFromCDS',
        direction: #DESC
    }]
}]
define view entity ValueHelpCDS
{
    ...
}
